the green knight is a fresh take on the  classic hero's journey  like with so many heroic odysseys the  green knight does many things but above  all else it is this  extremely and incontrovertibly weird  there are magic spells  ghosts giants spiritual foxes and  nightmarish fates  what in this supernatural world is real  and what is the imagining of our hero  circle wayne  the answer to that isn't immediately or  easily illuminated  similarly even the way the story ends  seems almost shrouded in mystery  not to worry though we can work the  strands of this strange tapestry  together until they weave a pattern that  at least makes some semblance of sense  the green knight is the tale of a young  man named gawain who just so happens to  be the son of morgan lafaye  and thus the nephew of king arthur and  queen guinevere the green knight never  uses these names other than gawain's but  as the tale is based on the 14th century  romantic epic sir gawain and the green  knights we can make some inferences  at the start of our tale gwen played by  deb patel leads a free uneventful life  full of wine women in song he seems to  spend more nights in the bed of one  woman in particular the vessel  played by elysia vikander who dreams of  being his lady in the courtly royal  sense  but it's not until christmas day that  the dye is cast  king arthur invites gawain to sit with  him in gwenevere while they discuss  the possibility that gawain might  someday have nightly tales to tell  dwayne's mother summons the titular  green knight who challenges all nights  in the hall to cut him with his own axe  and  in exchange have the same wound visited  upon them by the green knight in a  year's time  i will meet him you understand this  challenge  i did gwen accepts the challenge and  thinking he solved the situation chops  the green knight's head clean off  but the green knights is no mere mortal  so he picks up his own head and rides  away  laughing all the way and the knowledge  that he will kill gawain in a year's  time  this moment is so important because it  tells us what this incarnation of gwen  is all about  there are many fictional accounts of  gwen which portray him at times as noble  and at other times as graceless callow  and  utterly dishonorable the green knight  portrays gawain as a man manipulated too  easily by his own ambition  this gwain wants to have song song of  his gallantry and he wants people to see  him as honorable however from the outset  he seems more interested in perception  and power than he does with  the actual responsibilities of  knighthood when gawain arrives one year  later at the green chapel as the green  knight demanded acts in hand  hypothetically ready to be decapitated  there exists a duality of desire within  him one which wishes to die a hero and  another which wishes to live and become  king the end of the green nights is  about understanding the consequences of  both choices  the end of the green knight is split  into two sections what could happen  and what does happen in each gwain has  in his possession a magic belt that is  meant to protect him from any blow  and yet at first we see gawain distrust  his own magic and flee  reflecting the cowardice we see in him  throughout the story during his quest  wayne is defeated by three lowly thieves  we watch him accidentally drug himself  with hallucinogenic mushrooms  and we see him betray the word he gives  to a lord played by joel edgerton  as he keeps the lord's property and  gives himself over sexually to the  lord's wife who was also played by  elysia mcandrew  again and again gwen denies his own  knighthood when that title would get him  into trouble  and yet when gwen returns home after  running away and forsaking his word to  the green knight as well  he still accepts knighthood from arthur  as though he deserves it not only that  but gawain also takes a son he has with  essel leaving her forsaken  marries into royal blood and becomes  king a terrible king  dwayne's subjects despise him and while  his magic belt protects him he watches  his son die in his kingdom fall to ruin  in the end gwen dies a failure to his  name and his people with neither honor  nor nobility  and then suddenly we're back in the  green chapel as though nothing ever  happened  wayne's future a mere glimpse of things  to come in the face of that horrifying  destiny gwen removes his protective belt  and allows the green knight to lop off  his head  we get one earlier glimpse of this side  of wayne when he helps the ghost of  winifred find her own head at the bottom  of the lake  in that moment gawain helps winifred  find peace in the end the green knight  is about how it's better for gwayne to  die an honorable person than to live a  long miserable life  a stranger to oneself and a victim of  one's own most craven nature  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite movies are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  [Music]  you
 

